<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Experiments on Different Backbones</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">More experiments on the effectiveness of our method regarding different model architectures and sizes are shown in Figure <a href="#A6.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ F.2 Experiments on Different Backbones ‣ Appendix F Detailed Analysis and Comparisons ‣ JanusCoder: Towards a Foundational Visual-Programmatic Interface for Code Intelligence" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. We can see that our method can vastly improve the performance of various models across different benchmarks.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="A6.F7.2" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:178.9pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.23538v1/x2.svg" id="A6.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:247/184;" width="247" height="184"></object>
